       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily would give 15 g/day. For a 70 kg patient, that is above the single-ingestion toxicity threshold of about 150 mg/kg (about 10.5 g), and the patient would take it every day. I can't think of a clinical situation where this dose is therapeutic. It would risk acute liver failure and death.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 650 mg PO every 6 hours. Give me the dose and frequency you want.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If you're trying to get more pain or fever control, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen within limits plus another agent you choose.\n- **Route it through pharmacy.** If you think there's an unusual indication, a clinical pharmacist or toxicologist should review it first. The order would then go in through whatever process they set up.\n\nIf the dose was a typo or a unit mix-up (for example, 500 mg), tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
